ss-depth sections below already carry full provenance.\n\nDeciding where to go: each mapped area's narration tells you the SPAN of what lives under it; the area index names everything else. Expand a subtree when its narration (or name) shows your subject plausibly lives there — you'll get the trajectory, the variants, and the verbatim witness. But be strict about absence: if neither the map's narrations nor the index's names substantively cover your subject, it is NOT in this perspective — say so rather than expanding a loose thematic match (a word-overlap is not coverage). Decide from the map; expand to ground.\n\n# The map (steering grain)\n\n\n# Focus: document review, versioning, first version, reviewer assignment, editorial workflow (witness depth — per-call section)\n\n### ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst\ntype: ns__Decision\nXena: 'Every engagement starts with a diagnostic phase. Never propose solutions before understanding the system.' Two weeks, $5K, 8+ stakeholder interviews.\nDiagnostic First Methodology\nunder: ns__Strategy\n\n\n### ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst\ntype: ns__Decision\nXena: 'Every engagement starts with a diagnostic phase. Never propose solutions before understanding the system.' Two weeks, $5K, 8+ stakeholder interviews.\nDiagnostic First Methodology\nunder: ns__Strategy\n\n\nserved: ^ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst\n(pass this list back as `have` on your next expand — content you already hold is then returned as a bare ^pointer, never re-sent)","positions":"","pin":"f85a1447b500b423febca14373b8c382440f2fb7","positions_consult":"{\"positions\":[]}","context_bytes":2303},"live_run_id":"f87647b5b749","at":"2026-08-21T09:23:57Z"}
